b63fc157_7653357e",85,-2,1,"\"Disable\""],["f0c82165_bfcbc493",8,-2,1,"\"address autofill\""],["f1325fff_be8be3f3",58,-2,1,"```suggestion if (!prefs->GetBoolean(prefs::kAutofillProfileEnabled) && !base::FeatureList::IsEnabled( features::kAutofillAiIgnoresWhetherAddressPrefIsEnabled)) { MaybeOutputReason(debug_message,…"],["fe5e1e97_0dc5eeec",51,-2,1,"\"Autofill AI does\""]],0,479],[7142119,20405,33,2.122,1.642,[[10,0.811,214,28],[30,0.135,1,4],[1,0.054,66,1]],[["013da6fb_445641cd",88,-1,1,"In a few months this will hopefully be \"Improve enhanced Autofill\" instead and, in particular, won't have anything to do with whether this is enabled. WDYT about just calling it…"],["32dd6a30_51ca84f3",88,0,1,"non-synced?"],["49385cc7_b9263953",89,0,1,"nit: omit `k` prefix for consistency"],["a67ffc45_1344ac18",88,0,1,"should this be GetAutofillAiSyncedOptInStatus? The function name seems strange to me, because \"status\" in the end is not a verb like \"managed\" or \"enabled\"."],["dfe937cc_1e6d4dce",88,0,1,"should we have an \"autofill.\" prefix?"],["f6904c86_49141ded",88,0,1,"Can you document how these two interact? Why do we have two? Should `kAutofillAiOptInStatus` be synced? Should `kAutofillAiOptInStatus` be labeled as deprecated? Should there be a migration call?"]],0,480],[7146428,20406,186,7.323,5.882,[[10,0.881,215,165],[1,0.119,67,21]],[["73eacaa4_d743a952",52,-2,1,"I don't think this is the correct logic here. IMO it needs to be the following (pseudo-code): ``` PrefService::Preference* synced_pref = pref_service->FindPreference(kSyncedPref); if (synced_pref) {…"],["2e086553_19a23d72",51,-1,1,"Please update."],["626fbcc2_b6657b62",51,-1,1,"Please remove (I would understand \"set\" to mean that the local pref is set to the synced pref's value)."],["6a9f5e4f_5a1b6716",2,-1,1,"Please add a proper description."],["8bdf8d0d_aa9c798e",52,-1,1,"Isn't a synced missing here?"],["9c3eae63_9729a983",52,-1,1,"Please update."],["d0b22611_8b737594",52,-1,1,"This won't work - you'll have to go a level deeper and check whether the dict entries actually exist. I'll written a [small precursor…"],["f79fe878_5b2be53e",52,-1,1,"\"For the time being, it does not remove the old pref to allow rollbacks.\""]],0,481],[7130960,20410,10,0.384,0.302,[[28,0.667,1,7],[10,0.333,216,3]],[["18d92615_b4782075",33,-11,1,"You didn't add it to UKM"],["cc155736_392a36ed",33,-11,1,"You're not allowed to record the signature like that, instead, you need to hash it (privacy requirements). Here's an example."]],0,482],[7146803,20410,107,4.226,3.283,[[10,217]],[["4ea4e067_459e26ac",90,-4,1,"\"that it is\""],["593463de_10d3cd25",90,-4,1,"Same comment as above."],["e22cee2f_0dcbc6d8",58,-4,0,"For my own education: Could you check (e.g. with Marc) what happens when the user is not syncing? Is this just written to a local pref that gets synced when/if syncing restarts? What happens on…"],["f2455509_6e0eea93",90,-4,1,"Nit: `EXPECT_EQ(pref_dict.FindBool(signed_in_hash), false);` avoids crashing if the bool is not set and gives nicer error messages. But put differently: Is there any reason to look up the pref…"]],0,483],[7167229,20410,22,0.737,0.556,[[6,182]],[],0,484],[7167032,20412,11,0.451,0.307,[[10,218]],[["0829c986_0946961f",51,-1,1,"Could you add this to [debug features](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:components/autofill/core/common/autofill_debug_features.h) instead?"]],0,485],[7172417,20412,196,4.21,3.407,[[31,6]],[["63ac61f5_4c44d396",91,0,0,"Do you plan to add tests for this class?"],["95634e10_a228060b",92,0,1,"Should this be a `raw_ref`? I assume that we'll also need the same observer logic that we have for PDM, but it seems fine to start without that for now."],["cca859ad_1eaaaf75",93,0,1,"`CHECK_DEREF` once it's a `raw_ref`?"]],0,486],[7203167,20418,27,1.159,0.879,[[37,0.517,26,14],[38,0.483,3,13]],[],0,487],[7228762,20426,2,0.116,0.047,[[10,219]],[],0,488],[7204922,20427,192,7.323,5.882,[[39,0.885,0,173],[10,0.08,220,13],[40,0.035,0,6]],[["162df97f_e88055a9",94,-4,1,"@tchudakov@google.com: Is this the idiomatic way in Java?"],["26dc3d37_38f004ab",94,-4,0,"What exactly does this hold? - For a passport number, I assume it just holds the raw value. - What does it hold for names?"],["6433f456_fe249fe2",94,-4,1,"This was refactored back to primitive in a subsequent CL, but it could be done here."],["7f993844_2c87961e",95,-4,0,"How is this going to be used in UI? Will this string be concatenated with `Edit ...` or `Add ...`?"],["8d3e6d41_12286951",94,-4,1,"Let's use `java.util.LocalDate` because it consists of day, month, and year without a timezone."],["b40fe34a_b82244c9",96,-4,1,"Should be primitive."],["bb052c5e_b5ad0114",94,-4,1,"`@JniType(\"std::u16string\")`"],["c39e4b2c_4fcfe680",96,-4,1,"`JnitType(\"std::u16string\")`."],["e349c54c_b450f654",94,-4,0,"What does this do?"],["3da6e929_621aa472",97,-1,1,"This is the first build rule of this type that I could find in the entire Chromium source code. Are we sure that this is the right way to do it? Other Autofill enums are usually converted to Java…"],["7bf2c5ae_50e9abf1",94,-1,1,"double checking: are you sure you're going to pass `std::string` and not `std::u16string`?"]],0,489],[7205651,20431,228,7.323,5.882,[[10,0.532,221,121],[9,0.468,12,107]],[["79eac6b0_282177d5",98,-8,1,"Please drop (same below)."],["d2482a8e_3832e0a5",98,-8,1,"AFAIK we do not have this namespace elsewhere - could you drop it?"]],0,490],[7246045,20433,123,2.361,1.866,[[31,0.913,7,113],[39,0.087,1,10]],[],0,491],[7246714,20433,160,4.21,3.407,[[31,0.884,8,142],[39,0.116,2,18]],[["e4e6eefa_a37236fe",99,0,0,"I would not worry about saving bits for strings, let's convert all members (I just want to avoid weird side effects)."]],0,492],[7255955,20434,5,0.427,0.286,[[10,222]],[["8df83fe7_96e083ce",100,0,1,"For my own reference, is this going to be Android-specific feature or does it apply to more platforms?"],["fec02692_adc1ea3e",51,0,1,"Should this be disabled by default?"]],0,493],[